## Cloudflare Workers deploy (TanStack Start, Vite plugin)

TanStack Start apps run on Workers through `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` (set up in `vite.config.ts`), without Nitro. `wrangler.jsonc` points `main` at `src/server.ts`, the Worker entry that serves Start's handler{{#if (hasLibrary "evlog")}}; in an app with evlog it wraps that handler with `withEvlog` and passes the request logger as `context.log`. Call `useLogger()` from `@/lib/evlog` in app code{{/if}}.

**Build & deploy**
- `bun run dev` — `vite dev`, the app runs in workerd with the bindings declared in `wrangler.jsonc`
- `bun run build` — `vite build`, emits `dist/client` (assets) and `dist/server` (Worker)
- `bun run preview` — `vite preview`, serves the production build in workerd. Run it before deploying: `vite dev` hides errors that only appear once the Worker is built (see the global scope rule below)
- `bun run deploy` — `vite build && wrangler deploy`
- `bun run cf-typegen` — regenerate `cloudflare-env.d.ts` from `wrangler.jsonc`. Run it after install and after every change to bindings: `tsc` needs it for the `cloudflare:workers` module and the `D1Database` / `Hyperdrive` types

**Bindings and variables**
- Read bindings with `import { env } from 'cloudflare:workers'`. They are never on `process.env`.
- Declare bindings and non-secret `vars` in `wrangler.jsonc`. Local secrets go in `.env` (gitignored; do not add a `.dev.vars`, it shadows `.env`); production secrets with `wrangler secret put X`.
- Local state (D1, KV, R2) is persisted in the `.wrangler/` directory{{#if (isMono)}} at the monorepo root{{/if}}, the same directory the `wrangler ... --persist-to` scripts use.

**Global scope rule**: in a production build the app's modules are evaluated in the Worker's global scope. At module level there is no I/O, no timers and no randomness (`crypto.randomUUID()`, `crypto.getRandomValues()`). Code that does passes in `vite dev` and fails in `vite preview` and after deploy.
{{#if (has "database" "d1")}}

**Database — D1**: the app's `src/lib/server.ts` exports a `db` built once at module scope with `createDb(env.DB)`. The D1 binding is safe to hold across requests, so import `db` directly in server functions and route handlers. The `createDb(d1)` factory in the db {{#if (isMono)}}package{{else}}module{{/if}} stays a plain factory with no `cloudflare:workers` import.
{{/if}}

{{/if}}
{{#if (and (or (has "stack" "nextjs") (has "stack" "tanstack-start") (has "stack" "hono")) (databaseBinding "hyperdrive"))}}
**Database — Hyperdrive**: the Workers runtime cannot open a raw TCP connection to {{#if (has "database" "postgres")}}Postgres{{/if}}{{#if (has "database" "mysql")}}MySQL{{/if}}, and forbids reusing a connection across requests. The DB goes through the Cloudflare **Hyperdrive** binding (a pooling proxy), so the `db` package exports a per-request `createDb(hyperdrive)` factory — there is no module-level `db` singleton.
{{#if (has "orm" "prisma")}}
The Prisma client is generated for the `workerd` runtime (`runtime = "workerd"` in `schema.prisma`) and `createDb(hyperdrive)` returns a `PrismaClient` for the request. Scripts that run on Node, like `db:seed`, use the second generated client (`generated/prisma-node`) through `DATABASE_URL`.
{{/if}}

{{#if (has "stack" "nextjs")}}
- Build resolves the driver's `cloudflare:sockets` transport ({{#if (has "database" "postgres")}}`pg-cloudflare`{{/if}}{{#if (has "database" "mysql")}}{{#if (has "orm" "prisma")}}`mariadb`{{else}}`mysql2` with `disableEval: true`{{/if}}{{/if}}); the connection itself is created per request via `await createDb((await getEnv()).HYPERDRIVE)`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "stack" "tanstack-start")}}
- Build a client per request inside each server function or route handler: `const db = await createDb(env.HYPERDRIVE)`. Never create a client or read `env.HYPERDRIVE` properties at module level.
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "stack" "hono")}}
- Hono: build a client per request inside each route handler, `const db = await createDb(c.env.HYPERDRIVE)`, never at module level. Routes that query the db run under `bun run preview` (`wrangler dev`): `bun run dev` runs Bun without the Workers runtime, so there is no `c.env.HYPERDRIVE`.
{{/if}}
- **Setup**: `wrangler hyperdrive create <name> --connection-string="..."`, then paste the id into `wrangler.jsonc` `hyperdrive[].id`. `localConnectionString` is used by {{#if (and (or (has "stack" "nextjs") (has "stack" "hono")) (has "stack" "tanstack-start"))}}the local runtime of each app and matches your local `DATABASE_URL`:
{{#if (has "stack" "nextjs")}}
  - Next.js: `wrangler dev`/local only
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "stack" "hono")}}
  - Hono: `wrangler dev` only
{{/if}}
  - TanStack Start: `vite dev` and `vite preview` only
{{else}}
{{#if (or (has "stack" "nextjs") (has "stack" "hono"))}}`wrangler dev`/local only{{else}}`vite dev` and `vite preview` only{{/if}} and matches your local `DATABASE_URL`.
{{/if}}
- **Migrations** run on Node (not the Worker) via {{#if (has "orm" "prisma")}}the `prisma` CLI{{else}}`drizzle-kit`{{/if}} against `DATABASE_URL` — unchanged by Hyperdrive.
{{#if (has "stack" "nextjs")}}
- better-auth / tRPC over this binding (per-request consumers) is not wired yet — see #153.
{{/if}}

